From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: office <office@localhost>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] gridcraft: the default column width follows the Normal font

ECMA-376 18.3.1.81 and 18.3.1.13: the default width is baseColWidth (8) characters of the Normal font digit width plus 5 px, rounded up to 8 px, and stored widths (default and <col width>) are counted in that digit width. New workbooks (Times New Roman 12, digit 8 px) get 72 px; xlsx without defaultColWidth derive it from their Normal font; explicit widths are kept; Calibri 11 stays at 7 px. The .xls reader counts COLINFO widths in the digit width of its first FONT record (the Normal font), 7 px when there is none.
